<%#
  The interface language for someone without an account (a share link, the sign-in page),
  who has no settings to pick it in. A chip showing the current code, with the native list
  laid invisibly over it, so it fits a top bar, a sidebar rail and the dock alike.
  ?lng= is what i18next reads first and keeps in a cookie, so the choice holds on every
  later page; the rest of the address (filters, page) stays as it was. window.URL is
  spelled out because an inline handler looks names up on document first, where URL is
  the page's address as text.

  langPickerClass: colours of the chip, the shell's by default.
%>
<label title="<%= t('settings.language_label') %>"
  class="relative inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 h-8 px-2.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold cursor-pointer transition-colors focus-within:ring-2 focus-within:ring-current <%= locals.langPickerClass || 'bg-black/5 dark:bg-white/10 text-[var(--text-sub)] hover:text-primary-theme' %>">
  <i class="fa-solid fa-globe" aria-hidden="true"></i>
  <span aria-hidden="true"><%= String(currentLng).toUpperCase() %></span>
  <select aria-label="<%= t('settings.language_label') %>"
    class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-0 cursor-pointer"
    onchange="const u = new window.URL(location.href); u.searchParams.set('lng', this.value); location.assign(u);">
    <% Object.entries(LANGUAGE_NAMES).forEach(([code, name]) => { %>
      <option value="<%= code %>" lang="<%= code %>" <%= currentLng === code ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= name %></option>
    <% }) %>
  </select>
</label>
